# Build context excludes. Two purposes:
#   1. Shrink the context transferred to BuildKit.
#   2. Keep the `COPY . /app/.` layer's cache key stable across pushes that
#      touch none of the shipped files — docs, CI config, felt fibers, repo
#      metadata. When those are the only diff, `COPY . /app/.` stays a cache
#      hit, so `uv pip install -e .` and the (~2 min) image export are skipped
#      and the run is dominated by the test steps alone.
#
# Denylist, not allowlist: everything not named here still ships, so a new
# runtime-needed file can't be silently starved out of the image. Only add a
# path here once you're sure the image never reads it.

# Version control / repo metadata
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# CI / automation config (baked into the runner, never the image)
.github
renovate.json

# felt fiber store (symlinked in on dev machines; never part of the image)
.felt

# Documentation and top-level prose — not needed to build, install, or test
docs
*.md
*.rst
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
LICENSE

# Python / tooling caches and build artifacts
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
*.egg-info
build
dist
.coverage
htmlcov

# Editor / OS cruft
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
